#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Building-ROS-2-with-Tracing.rst:14
msgid "Building ROS 2 with tracing - how-to"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Building-ROS-2-with-Tracing.rst:17
msgid ""
"Tracing instrumentation is included in ROS by default on Linux, but some "
"systems need builds without tracepoint overhead or instrumentation. This "
"article describes how to rebuild ROS components with tracing tracepoints "
"excluded or tracing instrumentation disabled. After following these steps, "
"you will be able to validate the tracing configuration for your workspace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Building-ROS-2-with-Tracing.rst:27
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Building-ROS-2-with-Tracing.rst:30
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Building-ROS-2-with-Tracing.rst:32
msgid ""
"Linux ROS installations include tracing support and can be traced out-of-the-"
"box."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Building-ROS-2-with-Tracing.rst:34
msgid "Tracing can be removed at two levels:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Building-ROS-2-with-Tracing.rst:36
msgid ""
"To remove tracepoints, rebuild ``tracetools`` with ``-"
"DTRACETOOLS_TRACEPOINTS_EXCLUDED=ON``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Building-ROS-2-with-Tracing.rst:38
msgid ""
"For binary installations, clone ``ros2_tracing`` into the workspace before "
"rebuilding ``tracetools``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Building-ROS-2-with-Tracing.rst:40
msgid ""
"To remove both tracepoints and instrumentation function calls, build ROS "
"from source with ``-DTRACETOOLS_DISABLED=ON``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Building-ROS-2-with-Tracing.rst:42
msgid "Validate the result with ``ros2 run tracetools status``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Building-ROS-2-with-Tracing.rst:44
msgid ""
"Tracing instrumentation is included in the ROS 2 source code, and Linux "
"installations of ROS 2 include the LTTng tracer as a dependency. Therefore, "
"ROS 2 can be traced out-of-the-box on Linux."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Building-ROS-2-with-Tracing.rst:47
msgid ""
"However, ROS 2 can be built from source to remove the tracepoints or "
"completely remove the instrumentation. This guide shows how to do that. For "
"more information, see `the repository <https://github.com/ros2/"
"ros2_tracing>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Building-ROS-2-with-Tracing.rst:53
msgid "This guide only applies to Linux systems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Building-ROS-2-with-Tracing.rst:56
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Building-ROS-2-with-Tracing.rst:58
msgid ""
"Set up your system to build ROS 2 from source. See :doc:`the source "
"installation page <../../Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-"
"Development-Setup>` for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Building-ROS-2-with-Tracing.rst:62
msgid "Build configurations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Building-ROS-2-with-Tracing.rst:64
msgid ""
"The ROS 2 tracing instrumentation is split into two components: function "
"instrumentation and tracepoints. First, a ROS 2 core package (e.g., "
"``rclcpp``) calls a function provided by the ``tracetools`` package. Then, "
"that function triggers a tracepoint, which records data if the tracepoint is "
"enabled at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Building-ROS-2-with-Tracing.rst:68
msgid ""
"By default, if the tracer is not `configured to trace or if the tracepoints "
"are not enabled <https://github.com/ros2/ros2_tracing#tracing>`__, they will "
"have virtually no impact on the execution. However, the tracepoints can "
"still be removed through a CMake option. Furthermore, the functions can be "
"completely removed through a CMake option, which implies that tracepoints "
"are also removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Building-ROS-2-with-Tracing.rst:73
msgid "Building without tracepoints"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Building-ROS-2-with-Tracing.rst:75
msgid ""
"This step depends on whether you are :doc:`building ROS 2 from source <../../"
"Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup>` or using "
"ROS 2 binaries (:doc:`deb packages <../../Get-Started/Installation/Ubuntu-"
"Install-Debs>` or :doc:`binary archive <../../Get-Started/Installation/"
"Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary>`). To remove the tracepoints, (re)build "
"``tracetools`` and set the ``TRACETOOLS_TRACEPOINTS_EXCLUDED`` CMake option "
"to ``ON``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Building-ROS-2-with-Tracing.rst:80
msgid "Source installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Building-ROS-2-with-Tracing.rst:82
msgid ""
"$ cd ~/ros2_rolling\n"
"$ colcon build --packages-select tracetools --cmake-clean-cache --cmake-args "
"-DTRACETOOLS_TRACEPOINTS_EXCLUDED=ON"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Building-ROS-2-with-Tracing.rst:87
msgid "Binary installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Building-ROS-2-with-Tracing.rst:89
msgid "Clone the ``ros2_tracing`` repository into your workspace and build:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Building-ROS-2-with-Tracing.rst:91
msgid ""
"$ cd ~/ws\n"
"$ git clone https://github.com/ros2/ros2_tracing.git -b rolling src/"
"ros2_tracing\n"
"$ colcon build --packages-select tracetools --cmake-args -"
"DTRACETOOLS_TRACEPOINTS_EXCLUDED=ON"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Building-ROS-2-with-Tracing.rst:98
msgid "Building without instrumentation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Building-ROS-2-with-Tracing.rst:100
msgid ""
"To completely remove both tracepoints and function calls, :doc:`build ROS 2 "
"from source <../../Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-"
"Setup>` and set the ``TRACETOOLS_DISABLED`` CMake option to ``ON``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Building-ROS-2-with-Tracing.rst:102
msgid ""
"$ cd ~/ros2_rolling\n"
"$ colcon build --cmake-args -DTRACETOOLS_DISABLED=ON --no-warn-unused-cli"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Building-ROS-2-with-Tracing.rst:108
msgid "Validating"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Building-ROS-2-with-Tracing.rst:110
msgid "Validate that tracing is disabled:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Building-ROS-2-with-Tracing.rst:112
msgid ""
"$ cd ~/ws\n"
"$ source install/setup.bash\n"
"$ ros2 run tracetools status"
msgstr ""

